DEPLOYING

When deploying to heroku staging from development branch, `git push --force staging develop:master`
For prod, from master branch: 'git push production master'
For deploying the db: 'heroku run rake db:migrate --remote staging --app bcd-stg'
For restarting: `heroku restart --app bcd-stg`
For tailing: `heroku logs --tail --app bcd-stg`
For updating sitemap manually: `heroku run rake sitemap:refresh --app bcd-stg` (Change to sitemap:refresh:no_ping
    if I don't want to update search engines)

## Deploying to Digital Ocean:
To be able to deploy to production, you'll need to:
* add your public key to the server via the DigitalOcean web portal
* pull the branch you want to deploy
* be sure you have the production key set up at config/credentials/production.key
* Run the command:
```bash
bundle exec cap production deploy
```
After that has run, then run:
```bash
bundle exec cap production deploy:restart
```
Because I haven't 100% figured out what's going on, in order to deploy the latest
to production if the preceding doesn't work, after the `cap deploy` command completes,
you'll need to do the following as well:

* SSH to the server: `ssh root@192.241.140.249`
* switch to the rails user: `sudo su rails`
* `cd /home/rails/apps/brick_city_depot/current`
* run `RAILS_ENV=production bundle exec rake assets:precompile`
* run `sudo /bin/systemctl restart rails.service`
Then go check http://192.241.140.249/ in your browser. You may briefly see a 502
in the browser, try again every few seconds. It should come up.
## Notes on the production install
* Redis https://www.digitalocean.com/community/tutorials/how-to-install-and-secure-redis-on-ubuntu-22-04 and https://www.digitalocean.com/community/tutorials/how-to-install-and-configure-redis-on-ubuntu-16-04
  * cd /tmp
  * curl -O https://download.redis.io/releases/redis-6.2.14.tar.gz
  * tar xzvf redis-6.2.14.tar.gz
  * cd redis-6.2.14
  * make
  * make test
  * make install
* Postgres: https://www.digitalocean.com/community/tutorials/how-to-install-postgresql-on-ubuntu-20-04-quickstart
* rbenv https://www.digitalocean.com/community/tutorials/how-to-install-ruby-on-rails-with-rbenv-on-ubuntu-20-04
* Ruby 3.2.2
* npm `sudo apt install npm`
* Passenger/Nginx `sudo apt install curl git-core nginx -y`
Helpful: https://gist.github.com/deHelden/d18700a0996cd09d9321522c6c6af5a3
* If the bundle install dies, add some swap: https://www.digitalocean.com/community/tutorials/how-to-add-swap-space-on-ubuntu-20-04


